DIV and MOD by -1 of FIRST (INTEGER) and FIRST (LONGINT), and DIV and
MOD over every combination of signs.

Both back ends used the machine's signed division, and on x86
FIRST (INTEGER) DIV -1 and MOD -1 killed the program with SIGFPE.
MOD -1 is 0; DIV -1 overflows and wraps to FIRST, as unary minus
does.  See LLVM-IR-backend-docs/BUGS.md, bug 26.
